-- Source module: Solutions.KIL3Tab
/-!
# KIL3: a table of `W` streams on one stack

The `W` streams of the network are kept on stack `0`, one after the other (stream `0` on top):
`tab W F = F 0 ++ F 1 ++ ⋯ ++ F (W − 1)`, every stream of the same length `v`.

Operations (all `O(W · v)` item moves, plus the cost of the applied code):

* `applyC v w code`: run `code` (any stack-`0` program) on stream `w` in place
  (`applyC_runs`): the streams before `w` are parked on stack `15` and moved back.
* `copyC v w`: push a reversed copy of stream `w` on stack `16` (`copyC_sp`).
* `buildC v l`: push on stack `20` the (reversed) pointwise sum mod 2 of the streams `l`.
* `rebuildC W v T`: replace the table by the streams `w ↦ Σ_{w' ∈ T w} F w'` (`rebuildC_sp`).

Scratch stacks: `15` (park), `16` (copy), `17` (temp), `19` (zip out), `20` (new table),
`21` (loop counter).
-/

