/-!
# KFZ Desc: reading the chirp descriptor (register code)

The chirp descriptor on `cS` is `[K, p, α, h, d, b_0..b_{d−1}, s_0..s_{d−1}]` (`h = ℓ − 1`,
`t_i = 2^{h + b_i}`). **`setupP`** (one register program, leaf registers `4, 8–13`) reads it,
leaves `K, p, h, d, Σ b_i` on the registers `rgK, rgP, rgH, rgD, rgS` (scratch stacks
`55, 50, 51, 53, 54`), builds the chirp-table descriptor `descA 1 L ++ [2 ∏ t_i]` (`KFMU2.descT`)
on stack `35`, and restores the chirp descriptor (**`setupP_sp`**).
